<article class="env-definition" id="DBB342">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/DBB342">Definition <span data-tag="DBB342">4.4.5.4</span>.</a>idempotent!in an $\infty $-categoryretraction diagram!weakretraction diagram!small Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category. </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
An <em>idempotent</em> in $\calC $ is a map of simplicial sets $\Idem \rightarrow \calC $. We will refer to $\Fun (\Idem ,\calC )$ as the <em>$\infty $-category of idempotents in $\calC $</em>. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
A <em>weak retraction diagram</em> in $\calC $ is a map of simplicial sets $\Ret \rightarrow \calC $. We will refer to $\Fun (\Ret ,\calC )$ as the <em>$\infty $-category of weak retraction diagrams in $\calC $</em>. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
A <em>strong retraction diagram</em> in $\calC $ is a map of simplicial sets $\Idem ^{+} \rightarrow \calC $. We will refer to $\Fun (\Idem ^{+},\calC )$ as the <em>$\infty $-category of strong retraction diagrams in $\calC $</em>. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>